{"name":"Arctic Circle","hex":"#b2ccd9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Arctic Circle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The parallel of latitude that runs 66° 33′ 39″ north of the Equator, which marks approximately the southernmost place in the Northern Hemisphere where the sun does not set on the summer solstice and does not rise on the winter solstice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Arctic_Circle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Arctic Circle","blocks":[{"text":"The Arctic Circle is one of the two polar circles, and the northernmost of the five major circles of latitude. It is shown on maps of Earth at about 66° 34' N. Its southern counterpart is the Antarctic Circle."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Arctic_circle.svg/330px-Arctic_circle.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arctic_Circle","wikidata":"Q176609"},{"title":"Arctic Circle (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Arctic Circle is a Finnish-German crime drama television series that premiered on Finnish streaming service Elisa Viihde at Christmas 2018 and later on Yle. The series stars Iina Kuustonen, Maximilian Brückner, Pihla Viitala, Clemens Schick and Susanna Haavisto."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arctic_Circle_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q52261579"},{"title":"Arctic","blocks":[{"text":"The Arctic is the polar region of Earth that surrounds the North Pole, lying north of the Arctic Circle. The Arctic region, from the IERS Reference Meridian travelling east, consists of parts of northern Norway, northernmost Sweden, northern Finland, Russia, the United States (Alaska), Canada, Danish Realm (Greenland), and northern Iceland, along with the Arctic Ocean and adjacent seas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Arctic_%28orthographic_projection_with_highlights%29.svg/330px-Arctic_%28orthographic_projection_with_highlights%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arctic","wikidata":"Q25322"},{"title":"Circle","blocks":[{"text":"A circle is a shape consisting of all points in a plane that are at a given distance from a given point, the centre. The distance between any point of the circle and the centre is called the radius. The length of a line segment connecting two points on the circle and passing through the centre is called the diameter. A circle bounds a region of the plane called a disc."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Circle-withsegments.svg/330px-Circle-withsegments.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circle","wikidata":"Q17278"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Santa_Land_Rovaniemi_Arctic_Circle2.jpg/500px-Santa_Land_Rovaniemi_Arctic_Circle2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Santa_Land_Rovaniemi_Arctic_Circle2.jpg/1280px-Santa_Land_Rovaniemi_Arctic_Circle2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Santa_Land_Rovaniemi_Arctic_Circle2.jpg/500px-Santa_Land_Rovaniemi_Arctic_Circle2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Arctic Circle near to Santa Claus Village in Rovaniemi, Finland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASanta_Land_Rovaniemi_Arctic_Circle2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Polar_circle_monument_%2808%29.jpg/500px-Polar_circle_monument_%2808%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Polar_circle_monument_%2808%29.jpg/1280px-Polar_circle_monu